### =========================================================================
### 🎓 ADMIN — 401 vs 403 (authentication vs authorization)
### 📅 Day 46 · Phase 10 (Roles at admin)
### =========================================================================
### 401 = SINO ka? (walang login, sirang token, nabura ang account)
### 403 = kilala ka, pero BAWAL ka rito (hindi admin)
###
### Ang role ay binabasa sa DATABASE sa bawat admin request (hindi sa JWT):
### kapag ginawang admin o tinanggalan, AGAD itong tumatalab, kahit hindi mag-logout.
###
### Kailangan: isang admin account sa dev database —
###   npm run db:set-role -- <email> admin      (tingnan ang 04-register.http #8 at D-023)
###
### Code: backend/src/middleware/requireRole.ts · backend/src/routes/admin.ts
### Test: backend/src/routes/admin.test.ts · Diagram: docs/diagrams/13-rbac.md
### =========================================================================

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Walang login. Ang inaasahan:
###    401 { "error": "Not authenticated" }
###    🔍 Kahit sa path na wala (/api/admin/kahit-ano): 401 pa rin, hindi 404 —
###       hindi nalalaman ng hindi naka-login kung anong admin routes ang mayroon
GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/users

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Mag-login bilang NORMAL na user (mula sa 05-login.http — i-register muna roon kung wala pa).
###    Ang inaasahan: 200 · Set-Cookie: token=...
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "login-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Normal na user → admin. Ang inaasahan:
###    403 { "error": "Forbidden" }   — hindi sinasabi kung anong role ang kailangan
###    Sa terminal ng `npm run dev`: WARN Forbidden · event: "forbidden" · role: "user"
GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/users

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Gawing admin ang login-demo HABANG naka-login (sa terminal):
###      npm run db:set-role -- login-demo@example.com admin
###    Tapos i-send ito ulit — WALANG bagong login. Ang inaasahan:
###    200 { "users": [ { "id", "email", "name", "role", "createdAt" }, ... ] }   (page 1, hanggang 20, pinakabago muna — tingnan ang 14-pagination.http)
###    🔐 Walang password_hash sa listahan
###    Ibalik pagkatapos:  npm run db:set-role -- login-demo@example.com user   → i-send ulit → 403 agad
GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/users

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Mag-logout. Ang inaasahan: 204 → at ang #1/#3 ay 401 na ulit
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/logout
